Java 17 Features — Interview Focus ⭐⭐⭐

Java 17 is an LTS (Long-Term Support) release and is very important for modern Spring Boot interviews.

1. Sealed Classes ⭐⭐⭐

Allows you to control which classes can extend a class.

public sealed class Vehicle
        permits Car, Bike {
}
public final class Car extends Vehicle {
}

public final class Bike extends Vehicle {
}

Only Car and Bike can extend Vehicle.

Easy trick:

Sealed = restrict inheritance

2. Pattern Matching for instanceof ⭐⭐⭐

Before Java 17:

if (obj instanceof String) {
    String s = (String) obj;
    System.out.println(s.length());
}

Java 17:

if (obj instanceof String s) {
    System.out.println(s.length());
}

Java automatically performs the casting.

Interview phrase:

Pattern matching for instanceof combines type checking and casting.

3. Switch Expression ⭐⭐⭐

Actually introduced as a preview earlier and became a standard feature in Java 14, but you'll commonly use it with Java 17.

Traditional:

String result;

switch (day) {
    case 1:
        result = "Monday";
        break;
    case 2:
        result = "Tuesday";
        break;
    default:
        result = "Invalid";
}

Modern:

String result = switch (day) {
    case 1 -> "Monday";
    case 2 -> "Tuesday";
    default -> "Invalid";
};

You can also use yield for multiple statements:

String result = switch (day) {
    case 1 -> "Monday";

    case 2 -> {
        System.out.println("Tuesday");
        yield "Tuesday";
    }

    default -> "Invalid";
};
4. Text Blocks ⭐⭐

Introduced as a standard feature in Java 15.

Useful for multiline strings, JSON, SQL, HTML, etc.

Instead of:

String json = "{\n" +
              "  \"name\": \"Ashutosh\",\n" +
              "  \"age\": 36\n" +
              "}";

You can write:

String json = """
        {
          "name": "Ashutosh",
          "age": 36
        }
        """;

Much cleaner.

5. Records ⭐⭐⭐

Records became a standard feature in Java 16.

They are useful for creating simple data carrier classes.

Traditional:

public class Employee {

    private final int id;
    private final String name;

    public Employee(int id, String name) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getId() {
        return id;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
}

Using Record:

public record Employee(int id, String name) {
}

Java automatically provides:

constructor
accessor methods
equals()
hashCode()
toString()

Usage:

Employee e = new Employee(101, "Ashutosh");

System.out.println(e.id());
System.out.println(e.name());

Notice:

e.id()

not:

e.getId()

Interview trick:

Record = immutable data carrier

6. Strong Encapsulation of JDK Internals

Java 17 strongly encapsulated internal JDK APIs.

For example, applications should avoid relying on internal packages such as:

sun.*
com.sun.*

This improves maintainability and security.

7. Random Number Generator Enhancements

Java 17 introduced a new API for random number generators.

For example:

RandomGenerator generator =
        RandomGenerator.getDefault();

System.out.println(generator.nextInt(100));

It provides a more flexible way to work with different random number generator algorithms.

8. Enhanced Pseudo-Random Number Generators

Java 17 provides interfaces and implementations that allow applications to choose different random algorithms rather than relying only on java.util.Random.

🔥 Most Important Java 17 Features

For your Java + Spring Boot interviews, prioritize:

Feature	Importance
Sealed Classes	⭐⭐⭐
Pattern Matching instanceof	⭐⭐⭐
Records	⭐⭐⭐
Switch Expressions	⭐⭐⭐
Text Blocks	⭐⭐
Strong Encapsulation	⭐⭐
Enhanced Random API	⭐
🧠 Easy memory trick

Think:

Java 17 = Record + Sealed + Pattern + Switch

Java 17
   │
   ├── Record
   │      ↓
   │   Data carrier
   │
   ├── Sealed Class
   │      ↓
   │   Restrict inheritance
   │
   ├── Pattern Matching
   │      ↓
   │   instanceof + casting
   │
   └── Switch Expression
          ↓
       Cleaner switch
One very common interview question

Q: Which are LTS versions?

Common modern LTS versions:

Java 8
Java 11
Java 17
Java 21
Java 25

And since you're preparing around Java 17/21, the next important topic is the Java 21 features, especially Virtual Threads, Pattern Matching for switch, and Record Patterns.